ladon_appeal_tuning_20261011/\n  - #152 deep-search: C5五机制参数(选款周期/通过率/首单备货/Good档/破零/申诉时效)外部行业口径打底,学不到的标UNREAD → .agnes/work/research/celadon_mech_params_20261011/\n- [ ] 三个学习件回齐后:①各落框架§三十/三十一/三十二→v3.10+ ②把能学的落到工具/清单 ③明标\"学了就能干\"与\"仍要爸开口(9237/写动作点名)\" ④收工腿+独立多眼验收\n- [ ] 留队(非学习可解):NAS推(极空间客户端没起)、9237素材口开/渠道生死S2/内容资源S3(等爸拍)\n\n\nComplete every TODO update before starting the final user-facing response, and never call a TODO tool after the final response has started.\n\n\n<compaction>~53k tokens remaining</compaction>\n</turn-context>"}],"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_aigc__image_to_image","description":"Edit a reference image using original_prompt and enhanced_prompt. Accepts an HTTPS URL, local path, metadata JSON, or data URI; derives ratio when omitted. After registration succeeds, link the final Primary file path using standard Markdown.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ImageToImageParams","type":"object","properties":{"original_prompt":{"description":"The user's original image edit request before prompt enhancement.","type":"string"},"enhanced_prompt":{"description":"The detailed English edit prompt. State what should change and what must stay the same.","type":"string"},"reference_image":{"description":"Reference image as an https URL, local path, metadata JSON path, or data URI.","type":"string"},"size":{"description":"Optional image size accepted by the Agnes image API. Omit to use the default quality tier.","type":"string","default":null},"ratio":{"description":"Optional output ratio. Omit to derive the closest supported ratio from the reference image.","type":"string","default":null},"include_preview":{"description":"Reserved for future UI previews. Images are not embedded in tool results.","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["original_prompt","enhanced_prompt","reference_image"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_aigc__image_to_video","description":"Generate a video from a reference image and enhanced motion prompt. Accepts an HTTPS URL, local path, metadata JSON, or data URI. After registration succeeds, link the final Primary file path using standard Markdown.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ImageToVideoParams","type":"object","properties":{"original_prompt":{"description":"The user's original video request before prompt enhancement.","type":"string"},"enhanced_prompt":{"description":"The detailed English video prompt to send to Agnes Video, including camera motion.","type":"string"},"reference_image":{"description":"Reference image as an https URL, local path, metadata JSON path, or data URI.","type":"string"},"aspect_ratio":{"description":"Optional aspect ratio. Supported values: 21:9, 16:9, 4:3, 1:1, 3:4, 9:16.","type":"string","default":null},"seconds":{"description":"Optional duration in seconds. Supported range is 4-12; omit to use 5.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":null},"seed":{"description":"Optional seed for reproducible generation.","type":"integer","format":"uint64","minimum":0}},"required":["original_prompt","enhanced_prompt","reference_image"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_aigc__text_to_image","description":"Generate one image from original_prompt and enhanced_prompt. Saves it in managed image artifacts; after registration succeeds, link the final Primary file path using standard Markdown.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"TextToImageParams","type":"object","properties":{"original_prompt":{"description":"The user's original image request before prompt enhancement.","type":"string"},"enhanced_prompt":{"description":"The detailed visual prompt to send to Agnes Image. Preserve the user's constraints.","type":"string"},"size":{"description":"Optional image size accepted by the Agnes image API. Omit to use the tool's required non-pixel size tier.","type":"string","default":null},"ratio":{"description":"Optional aspect ratio. Pass only when the user explicitly requests an orientation or ratio.","type":"string","default":null},"include_preview":{"description":"Reserved for future UI previews. Images are not embedded in tool results.","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["original_prompt","enhanced_prompt"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_aigc__text_to_video","description":"Generate one video from original_prompt and an enhanced English motion prompt. Polls the task and saves it in managed video artifacts; after registration succeeds, link the final Primary file path using standard Markdown.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"TextToVideoParams","type":"object","properties":{"original_prompt":{"description":"The user's original video request before prompt enhancement.","type":"string"},"enhanced_prompt":{"description":"The detailed English video prompt to send to Agnes Video, including camera motion.","type":"string"},"aspect_ratio":{"description":"Optional aspect ratio. Supported values: 21:9, 16:9, 4:3, 1:1, 3:4, 9:16.","type":"string","default":null},"seconds":{"description":"Optional duration in seconds. Supported range is 4-12; omit to use 5.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":null},"seed":{"description":"Optional seed for reproducible generation.","type":"integer","format":"uint64","minimum":0}},"required":["original_prompt","enhanced_prompt"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_artifacts__present_artifacts","description":"Register and present existing local files as user-facing session artifacts. Call this tool directly, never through execute_typescript, with exactly one primary file, and wait for its successful Presented artifact result before claiming delivery; Agnes verifies the accompanying artifact_created event system-side. Use this only after the user explicitly requested a standalone, reusable, or downloadable file, an output file or directory, or a specific output file format. Keep ordinary plans, proposals, reports, tables, and drafts in chat. DOCX, XLSX, XLSM, and PPTX files must have the required OOXML ZIP package structure, not text or XML saved with an Office extension. For qualifying updates, reuse the same primary file path or stable dedupe_key so the previous artifact card refreshes. Do not register ordinary codebase edits, guessed paths, input or reference files, or files that have not been written yet.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"PresentArtifactsParams","type":"object","properties":{"title":{"description":"Human-readable artifact title.","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"Artifact type.","type":"string","enum":["slide","document","spreadsheet","research_report","image","video","html","data","other"]},"dedupe_key":{"description":"Optional stable key. Use it when later exports should update the same artifact card.","type":"string","default":null},"user_specified_output":{"description":"Set true only when the user explicitly asked for this artifact to be saved at a\nworkspace-external file path or output directory instead of the default workspace artifact\ndirectory.","type":"boolean","default":false},"files":{"description":"Files that make up the artifact. Use exactly one primary file and optional preview/export/manifest files.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/PresentArtifactFileParams"}}},"required":["title","kind","files"],"$defs":{"PresentArtifactFileParams":{"type":"object","properties":{"role":{"description":"File role inside the artifact bundle: primary, preview, export, manifest, thumbnail, or source.","default":null,"type":"string","enum":["primary","preview","export","manifest","thumbnail","source"]},"path":{"description":"Absolute or workspace-resolved local file path.","type":"string"},"mime_type":{"description":"Optional MIME type, for example text/markdown or application/pdf.","type":"string","default":null},"preview_type":{"description":"Preview renderer type: html, pdf, markdown, table, image, video, text, or external.","default":null,"type":"string","enum":["html","pdf","markdown","table","image","video","text","external"]}},"required":["path"]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_research__record_evidence","description":"Append one or more structured evidence entries to the managed research ledger. Batch multiple entries in evidence; returns quality warnings for hard-to-audit records.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"RecordEvidenceParams","type":"object","properties":{"mode":{"description":"Research mode. Defaults to deep_research.","type":"string","default":null},"evidence":{"description":"One evidence object, or an array of evidence objects to append in one call.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ResearchEvidence"}}},"required":["evidence"],"$defs":{"ResearchEvidence":{"type":"object","properties":{"claim":{"type":"string","default":null},"value":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_title":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_url":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_type":{"type":"string","default":null},"quote":{"type":"string","default":null},"observed_at":{"type":"string","default":null},"confidence":{"type":"string","default":null},"notes":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_research__write_research_report","description":"Write one complete Markdown research report and JSON manifest to managed artifacts. Include auditable evidence, conflicts, blocked sources, and honest confidence when available; returns local paths and quality warnings.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"WriteResearchReportParams","type":"object","properties":{"title":{"description":"Human-readable report title. If omitted, inferred from the first Markdown heading.","type":"string","default":""},"mode":{"description":"Research mode: deep_research or wide_research. Defaults to deep_research when omitted.","type":"string","default":""},"markdown":{"description":"Full Markdown report content.","type":"string"},"sources":{"description":"Optional source list used by downstream artifact consumers.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ResearchSource"},"default":[]},"evidence":{"description":"Optional structured evidence ledger. Important report claims should be backed by these entries.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ResearchEvidence"},"default":[]},"conflicts":{"description":"Optional contradictions or conflicting facts found during research.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ResearchConflict"},"default":[]},"blocked_sources":{"description":"Optional sources that were searched but could not be read or verified.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BlockedResearchSource"},"default":[]},"confidence":{"description":"Optional confidence label, for example high, medium, low, or unknown.","type":"string","default":null},"filename_hint":{"description":"Optional short filename hint. The final filename is sanitized.","type":"string","default":null}},"required":["markdown"],"$defs":{"ResearchSource":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","default":null},"url":{"type":"string","default":null},"note":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]},"ResearchEvidence":{"type":"object","properties":{"claim":{"type":"string","default":null},"value":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_title":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_url":{"type":"string","default":null},"source_type":{"type":"string","default":null},"quote":{"type":"string","default":null},"observed_at":{"type":"string","default":null},"confidence":{"type":"string","default":null},"notes":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]},"ResearchConflict":{"type":"object","properties":{"topic":{"type":"string","default":null},"variants":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"source_urls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"resolution":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]},"BlockedResearchSource":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","default":null},"url":{"type":"string","default":null},"reason":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__check_export_environment","description":"Check shared Node, npm, converter files, dependencies, and Playwright Chromium before PPTX export.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"AnyValue","type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__create_deck","description":"Create or reset the Agnes slide deck workspace under the current project.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"CreateDeckParams","type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string","default":null},"reset":{"description":"Replace the active slide workspace, cleaning its work files after the new workspace is ready.","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["title"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__export_html","description":"Publish the finalized HTML slide deck as the user-facing artifact when the user explicitly asks for HTML instead of PPTX.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ExportHtmlParams","type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__export_pdf","description":"Export a finalized Agnes slide deck to PDF (fixed 1280x720 slide pages). Requires an existing deck with deck_outline.json and confirmed_by_user=true. Do not use this for ordinary Markdown reports. Only when the user explicitly asks to export, convert, turn, save, or download a Markdown report as PDF, call agnes_artifacts__export_document_pdf instead.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ExportPdfParams","type":"object","properties":{"confirmed_by_user":{"description":"Must be true only after the user explicitly asked for PDF export or approved export after HTML preview.","type":"boolean","default":false},"filename_hint":{"description":"Optional output name. A trailing .pdf extension is accepted and normalized.","type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__export_pptx","description":"Export the finalized HTML deck to PPTX and automatically register it as the user-facing artifact. After a successful call, do not export again or call present_artifacts for the same PPTX.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ExportPptxParams","type":"object","properties":{"confirmed_by_user":{"description":"Kept for backward compatibility; PPTX is the default final slide deliverable.","type":"boolean","default":false},"filename_hint":{"description":"Optional output name. A trailing .pptx extension is accepted and normalized.","type":"string","default":null},"keep_qa":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"no_bg":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"bg_transparency":{"type":"integer","format":"uint8","minimum":0,"maximum":255,"default":null}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__finalize_deck","description":"Build the intermediate HTML deck files used for preview and export. Set final_output to the exact user-facing format that must follow: pptx by default, or html or pdf only when explicitly requested. This tool does not publish a user-facing artifact.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"FinalizeDeckParams","type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","default":null},"final_output":{"description":"Final user-facing artifact expected after finalization.","type":"string","enum":["pptx","html","pdf"]}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__record_source","description":"Record slide research notes, source URLs, or image references under deck/source. Prefer one call with sources:[...] for multiple assets. `source` still works for a single entry. For images, pass the exact local_path returned by image_search; this tool will copy/materialize it instead of requiring shell file operations.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"RecordSourceParams","type":"object","properties":{"source":{"description":"Single source entry. Prefer `sources` when recording several at once.","default":null,"$ref":"#/$defs/SlideSource"},"sources":{"description":"Batch of source entries recorded in one call.","type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SlideSource"},"default":[]}},"$defs":{"SlideSource":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","default":null},"title":{"type":"string","default":null},"url":{"type":"string","default":null},"local_path":{"type":"string","default":null},"slide_id":{"type":"string","default":null},"note":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__validate_deck","description":"Validate outline, slide HTML files, dimensions, placeholders, local image references, scrollable overflow, and source manifests. Structural failures block finalize/export. Visual-support notes are warnings: enrich those slide_ids in the same next turn with a local image or structured visual, at most 5 write_slide_page calls; they do not block export. When multiple slide_ids have structural failures, rewrite them with same-turn multi agnes_slide__write_slide_page in the next turn (at most 5) — never repair one failing page per turn.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"AnyValue","type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__write_design_system","description":"Write global visual rules to design_system.txt.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"WriteDesignSystemParams","type":"object","properties":{"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__write_outline","description":"Write the authoritative deck_outline.json for the slide deck. Slides must use the exact one-based sequence slide-001/index 1, slide-002/index 2, and so on; never use zero-based indexes or slide-01-style IDs.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"WriteOutlineParams","type":"object","properties":{"deck_title":{"type":"string"},"deck_goal":{"type":"string","default":null},"language":{"type":"string","default":null},"slides":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SlideOutline"}}},"required":["deck_title","slides"],"$defs":{"SlideOutline":{"type":"object","properties":{"slide_id":{"type":"string"},"index":{"type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0},"title":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","default":null},"key_points":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"asset_needs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]}},"required":["slide_id","index","title"]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"agnes_slide__write_slide_page","description":"Write one fixed-size 1280x720 slide HTML page with class=\"slide\". slide_id must exist in the outline. After materials are ready, emit remaining outline write_slide_page calls in the SAME assistant turn, at most 5 per turn, until every outline slide_id has HTML. Do not write one page per turn, and do not emit more than 5 write_slide_page calls in one turn (larger HTML batches hit the output token limit and become unparseable). First pass must include visual support (local image or structured visual) and no placeholder text. Prefer compact HTML. Optional sources[] records assets with the page. Use exact image local_path values returned by image_search/agnes_slide__record_source; do not invent source/images filenames. The page must not use scrollable overflow or clipped off-canvas content.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"WriteSlidePageParams","type":"object","properties":{"slide_id":{"type":"string"},"html":{"type":"string"},"sources":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SlideSource"},"default":[]}},"required":["slide_id","html"],"$defs":{"SlideSource":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","default":null},"title":{"type":"string","default":null},"url":{"type":"string","default":null},"local_path":{"type":"string","default":null},"slide_id":{"type":"string","default":null},"note":{"type":"string","default":null}},"required":[]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"analyze","description":"Analyze code structure in 3 modes: 1) Directory overview - file tree with LOC/function/class counts to max_depth. 2) File details - functions, classes, imports. 3) Symbol focus - call graphs across directory to max_depth (requires file or directory path, case-sensitive). Typical flow: directory → files → symbols. Functions called >3x show •N.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"AnalyzeParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"description":"File or directory path to analyze","type":"string"},"focus":{"description":"Symbol name to focus on (triggers call graph mode)","type":"string","default":null},"max_depth":{"description":"Directory recursion depth limit (default 3, 0=unlimited). Also limits focus scan depth.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":3},"follow_depth":{"description":"Call graph traversal depth (default 2, 0=definitions only)","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":2},"force":{"description":"Allow large outputs without size warning","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_skill","description":"Create a new reusable skill and save it to the user's skills directory. The skill becomes usable immediately via load_skill, or by typing $name in the chat input.\n\nBefore creating one, load the \"skill-creator\" skill for authoring guidelines.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["name","description","content"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Skill name: lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens only (e.g. \"release-checklist\")."},"description":{"type":"string","description":"When to use the skill. The model picks skills by this text alone, so state the trigger conditions, not the mechanics."},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Markdown instructions to follow when the skill is loaded. Use $ARGUMENTS where runtime input should be substituted."},"global":{"type":"boolean","description":"true (default) saves to ~/.agnes/skills for all projects; false saves to <working-dir>/.agnes/skills for this project only."},"argument_hint":{"type":"string","description":"Optional usage hint shown next to the skill in the $ picker, e.g. \"[file] [--strict]\"."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"delegate","description":"Run an ad-hoc task or named source in an isolated subagent. It sees only supplied instructions and context. Use async for parallel work, partition writes by file, and collect async results with load.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"instructions":{"type":"string","description":"Task instructions. Required for ad-hoc tasks."},"source":{"type":"string","description":"Name of a recipe or agent to run."},"parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"Parameters for the source (only valid with source).","properties":{},"required":[]},"extensions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Extensions to enable. Omit to inherit all, empty array for none."},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"Override LLM provider."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Override model."},"temperature":{"type":"number","description":"Override temperature."},"max_turns":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Maximum turns for this delegate. Overrides recipe settings.max_turns and AGNES_SUBAGENT_MAX_TURNS."},"context":{"type":"string","description":"Reference context to inject into the delegate's system prompt. Use for background information, file contents, or constraints the delegate needs but that aren't part of the task instructions."},"working_dir":{"type":"string","description":"Working directory for the delegate. Must be within the parent session's working directory. Defaults to the parent's working directory."},"async":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Run in background (default: false)."}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a file by finding and replacing text. The before text must match exactly and uniquely. Use empty after text to delete. In Full access (auto) mode, destinations outside the current workspace are denied without a confirmation prompt, regardless of user_specified_output. In approval modes, for an external destination explicitly requested by the user, set user_specified_output=true and wait for this call's confirmation; otherwise the edit is denied.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"FileEditParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"before":{"type":"string"},"after":{"type":"string"},"user_specified_output":{"description":"Set true only when the user explicitly requested this workspace-external destination.","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["path","before","after"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"encyclopedia_search","description":"Search Wikipedia for canonical background on people, places, organizations, concepts, and historical topics; use web search for current information.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"EncyclopediaSearchParams","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"Topic or entity to search in Wikipedia.","type":"string"},"language":{"description":"Wikipedia language code, for example en, zh, ja, de. Defaults to en.","type":"string","default":null},"max_results":{"description":"Maximum results to return. Defaults to 5, capped at 10.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":null}},"required":["query"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"entity_facts","description":"Fetch a bounded structured fact list for a known Wikidata Q-id. Use entity_search first when the Q-id is unknown.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"EntityFactsParams","type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"Wikidata item id, for example Q42. Use entity_search first if unsure.","type":"string"},"language":{"description":"Label language, for example en, zh, ja, de. Defaults to en.","type":"string","default":null}},"required":["id"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"entity_search","description":"Search Wikidata for an entity and stable Q-id. Use before entity_facts when the Q-id is unknown; never invent Q-ids.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"EntitySearchParams","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"Entity name to search in Wikidata.","type":"string"},"language":{"description":"Label language, for example en, zh, ja, de. Defaults to en.","type":"string","default":null},"max_results":{"description":"Maximum entities to return. Defaults to 8, capped at 20.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":null}},"required":["query"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extensionmanager__manage_extensions","description":"Enable or disable an extension by exact name. After enabling, continue with its newly available tools.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ManageExtensionsParams","type":"object","properties":{"action":{"description":"Whether to enable or disable the extension.","type":"string","enum":["enable","disable"]},"extension_name":{"description":"Exact extension name returned by search_available_extensions.","type":"string"}},"required":["action","extension_name"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extensionmanager__search_available_extensions","description":"List extensions that may provide a missing capability. Enable a relevant result with manage_extensions, then continue with its new tools.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":[],"properties":{}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"image_search","description":"Search for and locally verify web images. Prefer explicitly requested or configured image tools. Batch multiple subjects. Do not publish candidates as user-facing artifacts unless the user asked to see or save the images. For reports, slides, HTML, or other documents set source_material=true.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ImageSearchParams","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"Concise image query. Optional when `queries` is provided.","type":"string","default":""},"queries":{"description":"Multiple image queries in one call (internally parallel). Prefer this when several subjects need images.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"source_material":{"description":"True when the images are internal source material for another artifact. Forces publish_artifacts=false.","type":"boolean","default":false},"publish_artifacts":{"description":"Register verified images as user-facing artifacts. Defaults to true for direct image search requests. Set false, or set source_material=true, when gathering pictures for a report, slide, HTML page, or other document.","type":"boolean","default":true},"provider":{"description":"Optional provider: auto, bff, searchfree, searxng, or duckduckgo.","type":"string","default":null},"max_results":{"description":"Maximum images to return. Defaults to 8, capped at 20.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":null},"region":{"description":"DuckDuckGo/SearXNG region, for example us-en, wt-wt, uk-en, cn-zh.","type":"string","default":null},"safe_search":{"description":"Safe search setting: strict, moderate, or off.","type":"string","default":null},"size":{"description":"Optional image size hint: small, medium, large, wallpaper.","type":"string","default":null},"image_type":{"description":"Optional image type hint: photo, clipart, gif, transparent.","type":"string","default":null},"include_domains":{"description":"Restrict image source pages to these domains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"exclude_domains":{"description":"Exclude image source pages from these domains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"load","description":"List or load recipes, agents, and subrecipes, and inspect background tasks. With a task ID, wait by default; use peek to poll or cancel to stop it.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the source to load. If omitted, lists all available sources."},"cancel":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"For running background tasks: cancel and return output."},"peek":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"For running background tasks: check progress without blocking. Returns turn count, idle time, and recent tool activity."}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"load_skill","description":"Load a skill's full content into your context so you can follow its instructions.\n\nSkills are listed in your system instructions. When you need to use one, load it first to get the detailed instructions.\n\nExamples:\n- load_skill(name: \"gdrive\") → Loads the gdrive skill instructions\n- load_skill(name: \"my-skill\", args: \"the arguments for the skill\") → Loads a skill with arguments\n- load_skill(name: \"my-skill/template.md\") → Loads a supporting file","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the skill to load. Use \"skill-name/path\" to load a supporting file."},"args":{"type":"string","description":"Optional arguments to provide when loading the skill."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"platform__manage_scheduled_task","description":"Manage Agnes scheduled tasks. This is the task-oriented \"已安排\" feature, independent from recipe automation.\n\nActions:\n- \"list\": List all scheduled tasks\n- \"create\": Create a task with a title and prompt. Use schedule_kind=\"once\" with run_at for one-time reminders, and schedule_kind=\"recurring\" with cron_expression for repeating tasks. For reminder tasks, set prompt to the exact message Agnes should send when the reminder fires. Omit destination to use current_session in an ordinary chat or new_session in a project chat. Set destination only when the user explicitly asks to override that behavior. Do not pass a session id; current_session is always bound to the current chat by the backend. Omit provider and model unless the user explicitly names one; omitted values follow the user's active default provider/model at each run.\n- \"update\": Update a task\n- \"run_now\": Execute a task immediately\n- \"pause\": Pause a task\n- \"unpause\": Resume a paused task\n- \"delete\": Remove a task\n- \"kill\": Terminate a running task\n- \"inspect\": Get details about a running task\n- \"sessions\": List execution history sessions for a task\n","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["action"],"properties":{"action":{"type":"string","enum":["list","create","update","run_now","pause","unpause","delete","kill","inspect","sessions"]},"task_id":{"type":"string","description":"Task identifier for operations on existing scheduled tasks"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Task title for create/update"},"prompt":{"type":"string","description":"Prompt that Agnes should run for create/update. For reminders, use the exact reminder text to show the user."},"destination":{"type":"string","enum":["current_session","new_session"],"description":"Optional execution destination. Omit to bind ordinary chats to the current session and create a new session for each run from project chats."},"project_dir":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute project/worktree directory for create/update, only when the user explicitly requests project/repository/worktree context. Never infer from chat cwd; omit for chat tasks. On update, null or empty string clears project context."},"schedule_kind":{"type":"string","enum":["recurring","once"],"description":"Use 'once' for one-time tasks with run_at, or 'recurring' for cron-based repeating tasks. Defaults to 'once' when run_at is provided, otherwise 'recurring'."},"run_at":{"type":"string","description":"RFC3339 datetime for a one-time task, for example 2026-07-08T14:50:00+08:00. Required when schedule_kind is 'once'."},"timezone":{"type":"string","description":"Optional IANA timezone for display/context, for example Asia/Shanghai."},"cron_expression":{"type":"string","description":"For recurring tasks: 5-field (minute hour day month weekday) or 6-field (second minute hour day month weekday) cron."},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"Optional provider id to use when the task runs. Defaults to the current session provider."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Optional model name to use when the task runs. Defaults to the current session model."},"enabled":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the task is scheduled"},"paused":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether scheduled executions are paused"},"template_id":{"type":"string","description":"Optional template id used to create the task"},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Limit for sessions list","default":50}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Fallback UTF-8 text-file reader when shell fails or is unavailable. You MUST try shell first. Do not use it for binary formats such as PDF, DOCX, or XLSX; use a matching extension tool instead. Accepts absolute paths, including files outside the current workspace when the user provides them. Optionally start at a 1-based line and limit how many lines are returned.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"FileReadParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"description":"Absolute path to the file to read.","type":"string"},"line":{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-based).","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":1},"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_image","description":"Read an image from a local file path or http(s) URL and return it as image content for the model to inspect. Supports png, jpeg, gif, and webp.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ImageReadParams","type":"object","properties":{"source":{"description":"Local file path or http(s) URL of the image to load.","type":"string"},"crop":{"description":"Optional crop rectangle in pixels. Coordinates are measured from the top-left corner.\nuse to zoom in and get more details.","default":null,"$ref":"#/$defs/CropParams"}},"required":["source"],"$defs":{"CropParams":{"type":"object","properties":{"x":{"description":"Left edge of the crop rectangle in pixels.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0},"y":{"description":"Top edge of the crop rectangle in pixels.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0},"width":{"description":"Width of the crop rectangle in pixels.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0},"height":{"description":"Height of the crop rectangle in pixels.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0}},"required":["x","y","width","height"]}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_webpage","description":"Read one or more public webpages and return extracted text, quote candidates, and blocked status. Batch primary URLs; blocked or empty pages are not evidence and should not be retried.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ReadWebpageParams","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"description":"HTTP or HTTPS URL to read. Optional when `urls` is provided. Prefer `urls` for research.","type":"string","default":""},"urls":{"description":"Preferred for research Phase B: multiple URLs read in one call (internally parallel).\nUse this after search candidates are known instead of serial single-URL reads.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"max_chars":{"description":"Maximum text characters to return per page. Defaults to 18000, capped at 60000.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":null}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search","description":"Search file contents with cross-platform scope controls. By default, traversal stays inside the workspace, respects ignore files, skips hidden paths, and does not follow symlinks. Set include_hidden, include_ignored, or follow_symlinks only when those paths are relevant.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"SearchParams","type":"object","properties":{"pattern":{"description":"Text or regular expression to search for.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"File or directory to search, relative to the workspace. Defaults to the workspace root.","type":"string","default":"."},"fixed_string":{"description":"Treat pattern as literal text instead of a regular expression.","type":"boolean","default":false},"case_sensitive":{"description":"Match letter case. Defaults to true.","type":"boolean","default":true},"file_glob":{"description":"Optional gitignore-style file glob, such as \"*.rs\" or \"src/**/*.ts\".","type":"string","default":null},"include_hidden":{"description":"Include dotfiles and hidden directories. Defaults to false.","type":"boolean","default":false},"include_ignored":{"description":"Include files excluded by .gitignore and other ignore files. Defaults to false.","type":"boolean","default":false},"follow_symlinks":{"description":"Follow symlinks and junctions that stay within the workspace. Defaults to false.","type":"boolean","default":false},"max_results":{"description":"Maximum matches to return, from 1 to 1000. Defaults to 100.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":100}},"required":["pattern"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"shell","description":"Execute a shell command in the current dir. Commands run under `bash` (set AGNES_SHELL to override) - write command strings in that shell's syntax, which may differ from the user's interactive terminal. This platform does not expose the Windows `shell` selection parameter. Honor any user-requested interpreter/version constraints; report an unavailable or incompatible environment instead of silently switching interpreters. Inspect stderr and verify expected results even when exit_code is zero. Returns stdout and stderr as separate fields. Each stream is limited to 2000 lines; longer outputs are saved to a temporary file. Ordinary shell commands have network access disabled by the OS sandbox by default. Full access (Auto) mode or approval of this shell call enables network access for the invocation and its descendants. In other modes, set network=true to request network access for a call that would otherwise run without approval. Existing file restrictions remain in place. Managed CLI invocations retain their own execution policy. Hidden credential files or environment variables do not prove the host has no credentials.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ShellParams","type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string"},"network":{"description":"Request network access for this invocation; requires tool approval or Full access (Auto) mode.","type":"boolean","default":false},"timeout_secs":{"description":"Maximum time in seconds to allow the command to run before it is killed.\nIf omitted, defaults to DEFAULT_EXTENSION_TIMEOUT.","type":"integer","format":"uint64","minimum":0,"default":null}},"required":["command"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"todo__todo_write","description":"Overwrite the entire TODO content.\n\nThe content persists across conversation turns and compaction. Use this for:\n- Task tracking and progress updates\n- Important notes and reminders\n\nComplete every TODO update before starting the final user-facing response. Never\ncall this tool after the final response has started, and do not track writing,\nsending, or presenting the final response itself as a TODO item.\n\nWARNING: This operation completely replaces the existing content. Always include\nall content you want to keep, not just the changes.\n","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"TodoWriteParams","type":"object","properties":{"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"tree","description":"List a directory tree with line counts. Traversal respects .gitignore rules.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"TreeParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"depth":{"type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":2}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"web_search","description":"Search the public web and return titles, URLs, and snippets. Prefer explicitly requested or configured search tools. Batch known query angles; use research modes for broad evidence and read important URLs before relying on precise claims.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"WebSearchParams","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"Short focused search query. Use site:domain.com in the query for strict source targeting.\nOptional when `queries` is provided.","type":"string","default":""},"queries":{"description":"Multiple independent queries to run in one call (internally parallel). Prefer this over\nmany separate web_search calls when several angles are already known.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"provider":{"description":"Optional provider: auto, bff, searchfree, searxng, jina_search, exa_mcp, or duckduckgo.","type":"string","default":null},"mode":{"description":"Optional search mode: normal, research, deep_research, or wide_research.","type":"string","default":null},"max_results":{"description":"Maximum results to return. Defaults to 5, capped at 10.","type":"integer","format":"uint","minimum":0,"default":null},"region":{"description":"DuckDuckGo/SearXNG region, for example us-en, wt-wt, uk-en, cn-zh.","type":"string","default":null},"safe_search":{"description":"Safe search setting: strict, moderate, or off.","type":"string","default":null},"time_range":{"description":"Optional freshness filter: day, week, month, or year.","type":"string","default":null},"include_domains":{"description":"Restrict results to these domains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]},"exclude_domains":{"description":"Exclude these domains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[]}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","description":"Create or overwrite a UTF-8 text file. Do not use it for binary formats such as PDF, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, or XMIND; use a matching extension tool instead. Creates parent directories if needed. In Full access (auto) mode, destinations outside the current workspace are denied without a confirmation prompt, regardless of user_specified_output. In approval modes, for an external destination explicitly requested by the user, set user_specified_output=true and wait for this call's confirmation; otherwise the write is denied.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"FileWriteParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"},"user_specified_output":{"description":"Set true only when the user explicitly requested this workspace-external destination.","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["path","content"]}}}],"max_tokens":65536,"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true}},"request_meta":{"request_body_bytes":908963,"messages_bytes":862904,"tools_bytes":45938,"message_count":167,"tool_count":40,"model":"agnes-3.0-flash","stream":true,"near_body_limit":null}}